{
  "title": "Japan Weather in May 2026 - Agate Travel",
  "url": "https://www.agatetravel.com/japan/weather-in-may.html",
  "snippet": "Image 6: Warm May\n\n Tourists Wearing Kimono in Warm May\n Cities in central Japan, including Tokyo, Kyoto, Osaka, and Nara, enjoy warm weather throughout the month: daily highs hover around 20-25°C (68-77°F), occasionally nearing 30°C (86°F), while daily lows remain at 15-20°C (59-68°F). Relatively big temperature differences between day and night exist, so it’s advisable to dress warmly if you plan to head out very early.\n\n Southern cities like Okinawa experience early summer-like climate conditions in May. Daily lows generally stay above 20°C (68°F), while the highs typically exceed 25°C (77°F). Under sunlight, you might feel warm or even slightly hot. However, on cloudy, rainy, or windy days, the perceived temperature is lower. [...] Takayama22°C/ 71.6℉9°C/ 48.2℉04:48 / 18:51 69\nTokyo22°C / 71.6°F 17°C / 62.6°F 04:36 / 18:39 68\nWakayama23°C / 73.4°F 16°C / 61°F 04:58 / 18:52 68\nYokohama22°C / 71.6°F 16°C / 61°F 05:20 / 19:14 70 [...] In Okinawa, due to higher precipitation, sunshine hours are relatively short, averaging around 4-5 hours daily. Other regions generally see sunshine hours of about 6 hours per day on average. Additionally, except for the higher-latitude region of Hokkaido, sun protection is recommended in any other city you visit: this month, their UV index reaches around 9-11.\n\n Averages for Japan Weather in May\n\nImage 10\n\n High Temperature \n\n 23°C (73.4°F)\n\nImage 11\n\n Low Temperature \n\n 15°C (59°F)\n\nImage 12\n\n Rainfall \n\n 140 mm (5.5 in)\n\nImage 13\n\n Sunrise \n\n 04:27 ~04:50 \n\nImage 14\n\n Sunset \n\n 18:28 ~18:51 \n\nJan.Feb.Mar.Apr.May.Jun.Jul.Aug.Sep.Oct.Nov.Dec.\n\n The times for sunrise and sunset are based on Tokyo. \n\n## Is May too Late for Cherry Blossoms?"
